{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012Gy8GW2ppsbnomvaNcdTuB","type":"tool_result","content":"\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github/fake\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/gitx\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/gitx/gittest\"\n)\n\nvar bot = github.Identity{Login: \"ard[bot]\", ID: 4242, Kind: github.AuthApp}\n\ntype env struct {\n\tbare, clone, work string\n\tcfg               Config\n\tg                 *gitx.Git\n}\n\nfunc newEnv(t *testing.T) *env {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tbare, clone := gittest.NewRemote(t)\n\t// A dedicated clone supplies the object store, as the executor's does.\n\te := &env{bare: bare, clone: clone, work: t.TempDir(), g: gitx.New(\"\")}\n\te.cfg = Config{\n\t\tRepoDir: clone, WorkDir: e.work, RemoteURL: \"file://\" + bare, Bot: bot,\n\t\tBackoff: func(int) time.Duration { return 0 },\n\t\tLog:     slog.New(slog.NewTextHandler(io.Discard, nil)),\n\t}\n\treturn e\n}\n\nfunc (e *env) live() *effects.Live {\n\treturn effects.NewLive(fake.New(), e.g, e.cfg.Log)\n}\n\nfunc (e *env) main(t *testing.T, fx Effects) *Committer {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tc, err := NewMain(context.Background(), e.cfg, fx, e.g)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tt.Cleanup(func() { _ = c.Close(context.Background()) })\n\treturn c\n}\n\nfunc (e *env) head(t *testing.T, ref string) string {\n\treturn strings.TrimSpace(gittest.Run(t, e.bare, \"rev-parse\", ref))\n}\n\nfunc req(issue int, name, body string) Request {\n\treturn Request{Issue: issue, Stage: \"triage\", Role: \"lead\", Summary: \"update \" + name,\n\t\tFiles: []File{{Path: fmt.Sprintf(\".ard/%d/%s\", issue, name), Data: []byte(body)}}}\n}\n\nfunc TestCommitHappyNoOpDelete(t *testing.T) {\nfunc TestRetryAndConflict(t *testing.T) {\n\ttests := []struct {\n\t\tname    string\n\t\tk       int\n\t\tpath    string\n\t\twantErr error\n\t\tpushes  int32\n\t}{\n\t\t{\"one race\", 1, \"other/file\", nil, 2},\n\t\t{\"exhausted\", 4, \"other/file\", effects.ErrStaleLease, 4},\n\t\t{\"conflict\", 1, \".ard/12/issue.md\", ErrConflict, 1},\n\t}\n\tfor _, tc := range tests {\n\t\tt.Run(tc.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\te := newEnv(t)\n\t\t\tr := &racer{Effects: e.live(), e: e, t: t, k: tc.k, path: tc.path}\n\t\t\tc := e.main(t, r)\n\t\t\tres, err := c.Commit(context.Background(), req(12, \"issue.md\", \"mine\"))\n\t\t\tif !errors.Is(err, tc.wantErr) && !(tc.wantErr == effects.ErrStaleLease && errors.Is(err, effects.ErrNonFastForward)) {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"err = %v, want %v\", err, tc.wantErr)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif got := r.pushes.Load(); got != tc.pushes {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"pushes = %d, want %d\", got, tc.pushes)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif st := gittest.Run(t, c.l.wt, \"status\", \"--porcelain\"); st != \"\" {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"worktree dirty: %q\", st)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif tc.wantErr == nil {\n\t\t\t\tif res.Attempts != 2 {\n\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"attempts = %d\", res.Attempts)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tgittest.Run(t, e.bare, \"merge-base\", \"--is-ancestor\", \"main~1\", \"main\")\n\t\t\t\tif out := gittest.Run(t, e.bare, \"show\", \"main:.ard/12/issue.md\"); out != \"mine\" {\n\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"content %q\", out)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tif n := strings.TrimSpace(gittest.Run(t, e.bare, \"rev-list\", \"--count\", \"--merges\", \"main\")); n != \"0\" {\n\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"merge commit\")\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestRemoteRejectedNotRetried(t *testing.T) {\n\te := newEnv(t)\n\nA worker's inputs are `.ard-input/<issue#>/issue.md`, `comments.md` and, on a fix step, `test-output.log` (written by the loop, never committed) and `.ard/<issue#>/plan.md`. Nobody may change `issue.md` (only the scanner writes it, through the committer, not close-out), another role's file, any other file, or delete `plan.md`. A job that owns a `plan.md` section may add, replace in place, move or remove that section; a change to the text before the first `##` heading is allowed only when the job creates the file. Headings match exactly (case-sensitive), and `##` lines inside a fenced code block are text, not headings. A change outside the allowlist fails the job as `needs-human`: the comment names up to three offending paths, and only the redacted log is committed, never the offending files. A job with no valid role file still fails as `failed`, because the allowlist is checked after the role file parses. `logs/` is the controller's: files an agent writes there are ignored, not committed. `costs/` is the controller's too, but stricter: no role may write it, so an agent write there breaks the allowlist like any other path and fails the job as `needs-human`; the controller stages its own `costs/<job-id>.json` after that check, and it is never on `closeout.WritableFor`. The allowlist is code (`closeout.WritableFor`), not config; `plan_section` only names the heading a role owns. Workers and reviewers get their inputs outside `.ard/<issue#>/` (for example `.ard-input/<issue#>/`), because anything they write under it counts as their change. `issue.md` is the issue body without ard's cost block (see Guardrails), so the table never reaches an agent; the reviewer's untrusted `.ard/<issue#>/` input includes `costs/*.json`, which is controller-written and holds no free text.\n\nThe stage in a role file's name is the label stage (`triage`, `worker`, `review`; `config.Kind` and the role directory spell the last one `reviewer`), so a triage and a worker role with the same name never share a file.\n\nEvery `<stage>-<role>.md` starts with frontmatter the controller reads, so the agent reports its outcome without touching GitHub:\n\ncloseout/closer_test.go:170:\tt.Run(\"secret in plan.md\", func(t *testing.T) {\ncloseout/closer_test.go:173:\t\te.write(\".ard/7/plan.md\", \"## Implementation\\n\"+planted())\ncloseout/closer_test.go:184:\t\t\t\tif strings.Contains(c, planted()) || p == \".ard/7/plan.md\" {\ncloseout/closer_test.go:323:\te3.write(\".ard/7/plan.md\", \"## Implementation\\nthe plan\\n\")\ncloseout/closer_test.go:333:\te3.write(\".ard/7/plan.md\", \"tampered\")\ncloseout/closer_test.go:341:\t\tif got := files[\".ard/7/plan.md\"]; got != \"## Implementation\\nthe plan\\n\" {\ncloseout/closer_test.go:342:\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"committed plan.md = %q\", got)\ncloseout/closer_test.go:479:\te.write(\".ard/7/plan.md\", \"rewritten\")\ncloseout/closer_test.go:501:\tif !strings.Contains(b, \"write not allowed\") || !strings.Contains(b, \".ard/7/plan.md\") {\ncloseout/comment_test.go:38:\t\t\tReason: \"secret scan flagged .ard/7/plan.md (rules: github-token)\", LogPath: \".ard/7/logs/triage-lead-20260102T030405Z.log\"}}, false},\ncloseout/prepare_allow_test.go:40:\t\t{name: \"worker rewrites plan.md\", stage: StageWorker, role: \"engineer\",\ncloseout/prepare_allow_test.go:42:\t\t\t\tcommitBase(e, j, map[string]string{\".ard/7/plan.md\": basePlan})\ncloseout/prepare_allow_test.go:44:\t\t\t\te.write(\".ard/7/plan.md\", \"rewritten\\n\")\ncloseout/prepare_allow_test.go:46:\t\t\toutcome: OutcomeNeedsHuman, reason: \".ard/7/plan.md (not writable by worker:engineer)\"},\ncloseout/prepare_allow_test.go:67:\t\t{name: \"lead writes plan.md\", stage: StageTriage, role: \"lead\",\ncloseout/prepare_allow_test.go:70:\t\t\t\te.write(\".ard/7/plan.md\", \"## Design\\nx\\n\")\ncloseout/prepare_allow_test.go:72:\t\t\toutcome: OutcomeNeedsHuman, reason: \".ard/7/plan.md (not writable by triage:lead)\"},\ncloseout/prepare_allow_test.go:81:\t\t\t\tcommitBase(e, j, map[string]string{\".ard/7/plan.md\": basePlan})\ncloseout/prepare_allow_test.go:83:\t\t\t\te.write(\".ard/7/plan.md\", basePlan+\"\\n## Implementation\\n\\nsteps\\n\")\ncloseout/prepare_allow_test.go:85:\t\t\toutcome: OutcomeDone, files: []string{\".ard/7/plan.md\", \".ard/7/triage-engineer.md\"}},","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac259535-5641-4d6a-a5ca-6f814891f4eb","uuid":"569feadf-69a0-40e2-9e02-9f5d7955f55f","timestamp":"2026-11-23T13:36:02.630Z","tool_use_result":{"