{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKxDo6nacPtLTAaEbnWo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Close-out now merges a triage job's `plan.md` into the latest `main` copy when it commits, replacing only the job's own `##` section. A section another role committed after the job's base is kept. `go vet` and `go test ./internal/closeout ./internal/committer` pass. I did not run `make test` or `make lint`.\n\nI couldn't write one test that does the whole thing. The closeout tests use a fake committer, so the \"newer section on main is not reverted\" check is split in two:\n- **Merge logic:** a table test of `mergeOwnSection` covers a changed other section, a missing or removed own section, a fenced heading, and a duplicate own heading.\n- **Latest head:** a committer test shows `Merge` is called with the latest head's bytes and its result is what gets committed.\n\nOther points to know:\n- **Hook:** the committer's `File` has an optional `Merge` hook. It runs inside the commit attempt, so it runs again on each push retry against the newer head.\n- **Conflict handling:** if the `main` copy can't be merged, the job becomes `needs-human` with a \"plan.md conflict\" reason. The merge cases that fail this way are a duplicate own heading or a heading-like line in the own section. Only the issue is marked, and the log is not committed, the same as the existing commit-failure path.\n- **Signature:** `Merge` receives the job's own bytes as a third argument instead of a closure over them, as the plan sketched. This keeps the closure free of file reads.\n- **Docs:** `docs/proposal.md`, \"Who may write what\", describes the behaviour.\n\nThe report is in `.ard/138/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":844,"cache_read_input_tokens":52275,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_